name cfit-oberland
timeout 300

# THE PHYSICAL K.O., FLOWN — the one mission whose PASS is a crash.
#
# Course guidance has no terrain following (payerne-full.fbm says so in its own header), so a leg told
# to hold a FIXED altitude across rising ground meets it. Southbound out of the Kandertal at 2500 m
# ASL, the Bernese Oberland wall stands above 3000 m: nothing about the aircraft is special, nothing is
# disabled, the terrain is simply higher than the altitude the plan declares.
#
# READING RULE (binding): exit 2, `result=CRASH`, and a `monitor KO reason=CFIT` line before it. Any
# other exit means a physical K.O. did not end the run — which is exactly the defect this file exists
# to catch: until missions/FBMissionSim existed the BROWSER had no end rule at all and kept integrating
# a wrecked F-16 (doc/clients/clients.md §5.6).
#
# MEASURED (fb-gym --elev swiss, threads 1): KO at t=39.9 s, aglM -7.55 m, 46.4950 N 7.8998 E; the run
# ends on that tick and the RESULT line carries the monitor's own detail, "ground penetration".
# The same file in the browser: same reason, same detail, and the frame loop stops advancing the sim.

unit viper
  module f16
  spawn 46.58000 7.90000 2500 180.0 450
  wp 46.23000 7.90000 2500 450
